==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Mecha Dynasaurus Cat''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Dynasaurus Cat is a great anti-angel, with a manageable delay between its fiery attacks. It has the range to fight prominent melee Angels like [[Boraphim]] and [[Angelic Gory]] while the likes of [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen]] defend its small blindspot, or when paired with other support against [[Winged Pigge]], [[St. Dober]], [[Lutrinae Gokurakko]] and potentially [[Angelic Beast Rajakong]]. Thanks to its high [[Long Distance]] effective range, [[Angelic Sleipnir]] and [[Cala Maria]] aren't completely safe, even if it cannot outrange them, as its slow speed makes it less likely to wander into their line of fire. This piercing range also has the benefit of being able to snipe notorious enemy backliners such as [[Professor A.]], [[Camelle]], and many others in mixed stages. Its closely-spaced [[Multi-Hit|Multi-Hits]] generally shouldn't be an issue, as it does have the strength to ward off some, and most others will bear its full wrath. In general, it has only a few problematic matchups ([[Youcan]]/[[Sunfish Jones]], and many [[Wave Attack]] enemies), most of which can be resolved by other units instead.

Dynasaurus' own [[Conjure]] can also come into use. Admittedly, [[Knockback]] isn't a particularly strong effect, and it limits the unit's deploy count, but does provide a small burst of damage that can help regain ground. It has a somewhat short recharge time for its range, so replacements (and by extension its Spirit) are usually available immediately after a loss. It is also applicable for cheese timing, though other units fill this role as well.

The Multi-Hit it wields should also always be factored into when using this primeval destroyer, as sometimes its first hit will knockback angels and cause the other two hits to not land. However, this is much less of an issue for low-knockback Angels such as Sunfish Jones and St. Dober as they will be forced to soak up the fire. If accounted for properly, this dino can rampage through many Angel stages in the game, and has a bonus for working on mixed Angel stages.

